# Autonomous Vehicle Prototype - Systems Engineering

## 📌 Project Overview
This repository contains the Systems Engineering specifications, structural architecture, and 3D prototyping constraints for an autonomous vehicle. The vehicle is designed to track a 2cm black line on a grey surface and autonomously detect and avoid physical obstacles.

This project follows a strict Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE) approach using SysML, with a focus on physical prototyping, hardware interfaces, and Additive Manufacturing constraints.

## 📂 Repository Structure
* `/docs` - Contains the full Systems Engineering Specification (PDF/Word).
* `/cad` - Contains the manifold, watertight `.stl` and `.stp` files for the 3D-printed custom mounts.
* `/src` - (Future) Contains the Arduino microcontroller logic for sensor processing and motor actuation.
* `/diagrams` - Contains source code for PlantUML and Mermaid diagrams.

## ⚙️ Hardware Components
The system is strictly constrained to the following provided components:
* 1x Arduino Microcontroller
* 1x Motor Controller
* 2x DC Motors with tires & 1x Ball bearing front wheel
* 2x IR-Sensors (Downward-facing for line tracking)
* 2x Ultrasonic Sensors (Forward-facing for obstacle avoidance)
* 1x 11.5V LiPo Battery & 1x Breadboard
* 1x 10mm Plywood chassis

